What is yield()?

yield() tells the JVM:

"I'm willing to pause. If another thread of the same priority is ready, you may execute it."

Notice the word may.

The JVM can ignore this request.

------------------

Real-Life Example

Imagine two students sharing one computer.

Student A says:

"You can use the computer first if you want."

Student B may:

Use it immediately ✅
Say "No, you continue." ✅

Nothing is guaranteed.

That is exactly how yield() works.